{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured a persistent NFS share from node1:/srv/nfs/shared to node2:/mnt/shared. Both nodes use dataops UID/GID 4500; the directory is dataops:dataops mode 2770. Bidirectional writes preserve ownership and permissions. Both nodes were restarted sequentially and fully recovered with changed boot IDs.","actions_performed":["Installed nfs-kernel-server on node1 and nfs-common on node2.","Created dataops with UID/GID 4500 on both nodes.","Configured and enabled the node1 export, restricted to node2.","Added the persistent node2 mount to /etc/fstab.","Verified files created from both nodes are dataops:dataops mode 660.","Restarted node1 and node2 individually and verified persistent recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"NFS export on node1","command_ids":["cmd-1c33f6d32a204ccd","cmd-2dc19a9e0bb9426d"],"summary":"Shows the active export to node2, active server, and final healthy data."},{"requirement":"Persistent mount on node2","command_ids":["cmd-f7a6618439554df2","cmd-e1e593f49afc4210"],"summary":"Shows the live NFSv4 mount, persistent fstab entry, and successful post-restart access."},{"requirement":"Shared dataops identity and directory mode","command_ids":["cmd-1c33f6d32a204ccd","cmd-13667956db474a7c","cmd-e1e593f49afc4210"],"summary":"Confirms dataops UID/GID 4500 on both systems and directory ownership/mode 4500:4500/2770."},{"requirement":"Consistent cross-node ownership and permissions","command_ids":["cmd-b6c4f5e19ac84f6c","cmd-f559ed45037e43fc","cmd-2dc19a9e0bb9426d"],"summary":"Files created on either node are visible from both sides as dataops:dataops with mode 660 and correct contents."},{"requirement":"node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-068fa0a4ab484f2b","cmd-2219b43018a24c8e","cmd-5a5b8962914546a5","cmd-d82164d36832460e","cmd-ce303839b13a4151"],"summary":"Captures healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot ID, restored NFS service/export/data, and recovered client access."},{"requirement":"node2 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-ce303839b13a4151","cmd-72918bc0d39f49c3","cmd-309dcba0885e440f","cmd-e1e593f49afc4210","cmd-2dc19a9e0bb9426d"],"summary":"Captures healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot ID, automatic remount, successful post-restart write, and server-side visibility."}]}
